# What dinit starts at boot: the application, and through its dependencies
# everything under it — the mounts, then the clock, then the application.
#
# Nothing here restarts. Every service is `restart = false` (and dinit is built
# never to restart by default), so when the application or the clock keeper
# ends, what depends on it stops, this stops, and with every service stopped
# dinit — started with `--auto-recovery` from the command line — starts
# `recovery`, which powers the guest off. A run that cannot continue should stop
# existing; there is no in-place recovery in this design.
type = internal
depends-on: app
